.TH WPEDIT 1 "23 September 2011" Linux "FPAC Operator's Manual"
.SH NAME 
wpedit \- FPAC White Pages database editor.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wpedit
[\-c] [\-v]
.I callsign
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
.B wpedit
opens an edit session for a callsign record present in the FPAC WP database.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP 20
.B \-c
End the lines with a carriage return only, as a packet radio terminal
expects, instead of a line feed.
.TP 20
.B \-v
Verbose: report the White Pages server calls in the system log.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP 20
.BI "\-a   rose_address"
Change the ROSE address
.TP 20
.BI "\-b"
Bye (exit editor)
.TP 20
.BI "\-d   digi_path"
Change the Digi path. Use d . to remove the digi path.
.TP 20
.BI "\-n"
Toggle the record between User and Node.
.TP 20
.BI "\-u"
Undelete. Restore a deleted record
.TP 20
.BI "\-r"
Mark the record for removal.
.SH AUTHOR
